From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chenyk <chenyk@gl-inet.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 104/105] perf: reduce ovpn hot-path locking and copies

Reduce hot-path contention in the ovpn-dco data path:

* add per-worker queues to encrypt/decrypt ctx for TCP parallel paths
* UDP RX/TX keeps using shared queues for natural work-stealing balance
* decrypt worker: drain per-worker queue first, then shared queue
* encrypt worker: drain per-worker queue first, then shared queue
* skip UDP endpoint lock/update when the peer endpoint is unchanged
* reuse complete TCP strparser skbs when they are linear and unshared
* clear crypto_tmp on pre-submit AEAD errors to keep post cleanup safe

Signed-off-by: chenyk <chenyk@gl-inet.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ovpn/crypto_aead.c	2026-05-20 14:21:46.363784327 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ovpn/crypto_aead.c	2026-05-20 14:20:58.460016883 +0800
@@ -134,6 +134,17 @@
 			     __alignof__(struct scatterlist));
 }
 
+static void ovpn_aead_crypto_tmp_free(struct sk_buff *skb)
+{
+	void *tmp = ovpn_skb_cb(skb)->crypto_tmp;
+
+	if (!tmp)
+		return;
+
+	kmem_cache_free(ovpn_crypto_tmp_cache, tmp);
+	ovpn_skb_cb(skb)->crypto_tmp = NULL;
+}
